hkeepsie has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Poughkeepsie's nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1983.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 40\u00b0F was the 10th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 93 since 1931, the coolest since 2019.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 89% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>40\u00b0F</strong> was the 10th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 93 since 1931, the coolest since 2019. The normal high for the date is 52\u00b0F, and the record is 73\u00b0F (1964). The low of <strong>35\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Poughkeepsie has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Poughkeepsie's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Poughkeepsie has set <strong class=\"sig\">40 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 103 that chance alone would give, and <strong>111 record highs</strong>, close to the 103 that chance alone would give. The 1940s hold the most record highs of any decade (64). Poughkeepsie's all-time high is 104\u00b0F, on August 1, 1933.","t_chg":"Poughkeepsie's nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1983.","p_chg":"Across 92 complete years: Poughkeepsie's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.02 to +0.25), about +1.3\u00b0F since 1931. Poughkeepsie's average high shows no clear change: +0.11\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.22) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1983, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.94\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.68 to +1.21) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.83\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.51 to +1.14). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Poughkeepsie's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.25 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 42.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (62.01 in); the driest, 1964 (24.52 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}